course: dictionary
lesson: 15243
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the writer means. Sheriff is one of these words.
explain: «The town sheriff rode into the dusty street, and everyone stepped aside.» The dusty street and the riding are Wild West clues, so here a sheriff is the lawman of a town.
explain: «The judge gave her verdict in the sheriff's court in Glasgow.» A court and a judge point to Scotland, where a sheriff is a judge. Always ask which meaning fits the place and the job in the sentence.
fact: A sheriff is the chief police officer of a county in the USA.
fact: In Wild West stories, the sheriff is the lawman of a town.
fact: In Scotland, a sheriff is a judge.
fact: In England and Wales, a sheriff has a ceremonial job, which means a special official job with old traditions.
fact: Sheriffs in the USA are elected, which means people vote for them.
exercise: «The sheriff rode into town on his horse, and the outlaws ran away.» In this story, what is a sheriff? | *The lawman of a town | A type of horse | A judge in a Scottish court | A bank robber
exercise: «The sheriff in Scotland read out the court's decision.» Which meaning is this? | A helper of the police | The lawman of a Wild West town | *A judge in Scotland | A ceremonial official in England
exercise: Mia found a shiny badge that said deputy sheriff. What is a deputy sheriff? | A famous villain in a story | A king's servant | *A helper of the sheriff | A horse that runs very fast
test: «In the USA, the sheriff of the county is chosen by votes.» What does this tell you about sheriffs in the USA? | They are always kings | They are never chosen by anyone | *They are elected, so people vote for them | They only work in Scotland
test: Tom reads about «the Sheriff of Nottingham» in a Robin Hood story. What kind of sheriff is this? | *A villain in an old legend | An elected police chief in the USA | A judge in a Scottish court | A cowboy lawman in a film
exam: Jack reads «The sheriff tipped his hat and smiled.» Which meaning fits best, and what clue helped you? | A bank robber, because he smiled | A horse, because it tipped its head | A judge in a Scottish court, because judges wear hats | *A lawman of a town, because the hat and the smile suit a Wild West story
